	"description": [
		"In this final semester in Asian Conversations students examine modern reinterpretations of traditional Asia focusing on major social and cultural aspects of the 19th through 21st centuries. Students engage with primary and secondary texts through written and oral presentation, including materials collected during Interim. Offered annually in the spring semester. Prerequisite: CHIN 231 or JAPAN 231 and ASIAN 215 or ASIAN 216."
